      "id": 1,
      "text": "Beulah’s post office opened in 1886, founded by William Z. Sturgeon on his land in Spring Creek Township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/beulah_missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "An early postmaster named the community after his daughter, giving Beulah its personal touch.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beulah%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Beulah straddles the Texas–Phelps county line and borders the Mark Twain National Forest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/beulah_missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By the early 1900s, Beulah boasted a general store, grist mill, blacksmith shops, a bank, and a one‑room schoolhouse.",
